    "image": "/blog/articles/gta-6-eight-game-awards-nominations.jpg",
    "imageAlt": "Pinterest photo of The Game Awards golden statue and ceremony stage",
    "body": "<p>Grand Theft Auto 6 has claimed eight nominations at The Game Awards 2026, putting Rockstar Games at the top of the ballot two days ahead of the game's November 19 console release. Announced on November 17 ahead of the December 10 ceremony at the Peacock Theater in Los Angeles, the haul confirms that critics who received pre-launch review builds came away deeply impressed.</p><p>Leading the list is Game of the Year, where GTA 6 faces a stacked field alongside 007 First Light, Control Resonant, Phantom Blade Zero, Resident Evil Requiem, and Ocarina of Time Remake. Because The Game Awards eligibility window covers games released and reviewed before its mid-November cutoff, Rockstar's Thursday launch landed just inside the wire for jury voting.</p><h2>Creative craft and the breakout acting nod</h2><p>Beyond the headline trophy, GTA 6 picked up nominations for Best Game Direction, Best Narrative, Best Art Direction, and Best Score and Music. Together, those four categories point to how voters responded to the scope of Leonida: not just as a technical sandbox, but as a tightly directed character drama backed by a sprawling radio and score soundtrack. The remaining nods round out its recognition across technical and genre craft on the 2026 ballot.</p><p>The biggest talking point, however, sits in Best Performance. Actress Manni L. Perez earned a nomination for her work in GTA 6, effectively ending years of community detective work and confirming her role as co-protagonist Lucia. Rockstar rarely spotlights individual cast members ahead of launch, making the jury nomination an unusually public curtain call.</p><h2>What eight nods mean heading into December 10</h2><p>Leading the nomination count never guarantees a clean sweep, especially when voters split ballots across major releases from Capcom, Remedy, and Nintendo. Still, GTA 6 enters December 10 with enormous cultural momentum. Once millions of PS5 and Xbox Series X|S players actually step into Vice City this week, the public fan vote portion of the awards will only amplify the spotlight.</p>"
