    "title": "GTA 6 Gameplay Features: 10 Details Players Should Know",
    "seoTitle": "GTA 6 Gameplay Features: 10 Confirmed Details Before Launch | Bugwrite",
    "metaDescription": "Before GTA 6 unlocks on November 19, here are 10 confirmed gameplay, world, customization, and platform details every PS5 and Xbox Series X|S player should know.",
    "keywords": [
      "GTA 6 gameplay features",
      "GTA 6 details",
      "Rideout Customs GTA 6",
      "Sara's Unisex Salon",
      "GTA 6 Leonida gameplay"
    ],
    "dek": "From dual-protagonist dynamics and six distinct biomes to car shops, salons, and safehouse upgrades, here is what defines day one in Leonida.",
    "author": "Jordan Kim",
    "authorRole": "Games & Hardware Reporter",
    "publishedAgo": "8 hours ago",
    "publishedDate": "Nov 18, 2026",
    "readTime": "4 min read",
    "image": "/blog/articles/gta-6-gameplay-features-details.jpg",
    "imageAlt": "Pinterest photo of luxury speedboat cruising turquoise Vice City waters",
    "body": "<p>With Grand Theft Auto 6 unlocking on November 19, Rockstar has kept tight control over raw unedited gameplay, yet its trailers, regional breakdowns, and official edition listings already confirm ten concrete pillars shaping how Leonida plays on day one. First and foremost is the dual-protagonist structure starring Jason and Lucia, anchoring the campaign around a tightly linked criminal pair rather than a trio. Second is the scale of the State of Leonida itself, spanning six distinct regions: Vice City, the Leonida Keys, the Grassrivers wetlands, Port Gellhorn, industrial Ambrosia, and Mount Kalaga National Park.</p><p>Third is terrain diversity driving vehicle choice. Navigating Ocean Beach boulevards, island causeways, airboat-friendly swamps, and mountain trails means players will lean on a much broader garage, reflected in confirmed rides like the '95 Grotti Cheetah and the off-road '67 Vapid Dominator Buggy. Fourth is dedicated vehicle storage right from the start for early buyers, highlighted by properties like the Shoreline Court Garage.</p><h2>Customization, nightlife, and safehouses</h2><p>Fifth and sixth come directly from Rockstar's confirmed in-world businesses: Rideout Customs handles deep vehicle modification, while Sara's Unisex Salon brings dedicated character styling for hair and grooming alongside expanded apparel options. Seventh is safehouse progression, with Rockstar explicitly confirming safehouse upgrades as part of its story-mode ecosystem, turning home bases into functional hubs rather than simple save spots.</p><p>Eighth is Vice City's denser interior and nightlife scene, spotlighted by named destinations such as the NINE1NINE nightclub, Jack of Hearts, and transit landmarks like Vice City International Airport. Together, they signal a map packed with social spaces to visit between story jobs.</p><h2>Current-gen scale and ecosystem hooks</h2><p>Ninth is current-generation console exclusivity at launch. Built strictly for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S with a roughly 212 GB install size, GTA 6 leaves legacy PS4 and Xbox One hardware behind to stream denser crowds and lighting seamlessly. Tenth is tighter integration with GTA+, bundled for one month with pre-orders, signaling how Rockstar plans to support Leonida well beyond launch week.</p>"
